    'GLM5.3(Max)V2': { title: 'Solar System Motion Model · Solar System' , note: "This online Three.js build uses full JPL secular elements, a normalized Kepler solver, and shared sampling for matching paths. Seven moons, genuine Halley, a moving small-body belt, Bloom/ACES, and 4× scene MSAA are implemented. The Moon explicitly uses the untilted Earth system with a 5.14-degree ecliptic inclination; Triton uses a negative period and 23-degree tilt only once."},
    'GLM5.3(Max)V3': { title: 'Solar System Motion Model · WebGL2' , note: "This offline WebGL2 build has JPL secular elements, Kepler solving, matching paths, two moving belts, Halley/Encke, Bloom/ACES, and follow. Of ten moons, the Moon is incorrectly equatorial; the other nine parent-relative circles, including correctly retrograde Triton, remain valid."},
    'GLM5.3(Max)V1-TasksAssignedByOpus5': { title: 'Solar System · Real-Time Motion Model' , note: "Source and pure-function review: 1 of eight implemented moons pass the signed-normal/entity checks. Visual appearance is excluded. Elements, moving belts, atmosphere and post-processing work. Only Triton has the required signed orbital direction. Now resets the date alone; the Halley date claim is inconsistent."},
    'GLM5.3(Max)V2-TasksAssignedByOpus5': { title: 'Real-Time Solar System Model v4' , note: "Source and pure-function review: 0 of eight implemented moons pass the signed-normal/entity checks. Visual appearance is excluded. The pipeline includes MSAA and ring shadows. A LINEAR resolve alone is not a fatal finding: the parent runtime reports continued rendering and zero GL errors. Actual moon normals fail the required directions."},
