    'KimiK3Max-TasksAssignedByOpus5': { title: 'Solar System · Real-Time Orbital Model' , note: "Source and pure-function review: 8 of eight implemented moons pass the signed-normal/entity checks. Visual appearance is excluded. Negative local Z with the actual right-handed basis preserves all eight moon directions. Triton uses a 23.1-degree plane with negative period correctly. Zoom can enter bodies and Now resets only time."},
    'KimiK3Max': { title: 'Solar System Simulator' , note: "This online Three.js build uses measured fixed J2000 elements and a robust Kepler solver, with matching paths, two moving belts, genuine Halley, Bloom/ACES, focus, and follow. Of seven moons, the Moon is incorrectly equatorial and Triton omits its roughly 23-degree inclination; the other five parent-relative circles remain valid."},
    'KimiK3(Max)V2-TasksAssignedByOpus5': { title: 'Real-Time Solar System Model' , note: "Source and pure-function review: 1 of eight implemented moons pass the signed-normal/entity checks. Visual appearance is excluded. Only half the generated satellite orbit vertices are drawn. Tail vertex data violate their declared stride. Moon direction defects are scored per moon; approximate distance displays and the Halley date are separate data problems."},
    'KimiK3(Max)V2': { title: 'Solar System' , note: "This offline WebGL2 build uses JPL secular elements, Kepler solving, and shared orbit sampling, with a moving belt, real Bloom/ACES, and continuous focus-follow. It supports float HDR, an RGBA8 fallback, and multisampling. Its eight moons use measured radii and periods but randomized orbital inclinations and nodes; the Moon additionally applies its ecliptic 5."},
